      "writtenOn": "2021-05-17T11:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have used formula R1 \u003d R0*exp(B * (1/T1 - 1/T0) to get resistance of thermistor at temperature T1. T0 is given 25 *C \u003d 298,15 K, B and R0 are given in thermistor specification.\n\nNext I computed Vout from voltage divider using formula Vout \u003d (Vdd * R1)/(R + R1) where Vdd and R are given for thermistor and R1 are resistances at different temperatures which I computed in first step.\n\nFormula from first step comes from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermistor#B_or_%CE%B2_parameter_equation",
      "parentUuid": "ef630c12_9b9678a9",
      "revId": "9c67cd542003621debd17a73dd0a91dc717bc6c2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a154b2a5_2d6834d0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-17T15:51:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added the formula version to the spreadsheet that I shared with you.\n\nWhen I calculated these, I used a resistance lookup table by a thermistor manufacture since the B values isn\u0027t constant through the entire range.\n\nFor example search for \"B473\" in https://www.murata.com/~/media/webrenewal/support/library/catalog/products/thermistor/ntc/r44e.ashx\n\nand you will find a resistance lookup table for a few different B4050 47K thermistors. The table data in this datasheet is closer to the values in the original table based calculations than the formula based data (using a constant B).\n\nI am not convinced we should update these tables",
      "parentUuid": "326a46fc_6ce097bf",
      "revId": "9c67cd542003621debd17a73dd0a91dc717bc6c2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
